  "next_id": 79,
  "comments": "Mirror Transport Museum. Modest Mussorgsky, Pictures at an Exhibition, Promenade I. Quarter note = 40 throughout. Two beats of low bowed B-flat introduce the clarinet. The low clarinet sings the opening. The harp plays quiet chord tones on beats one and four. In bars 9–13 it takes the opening theme in D-flat and sings the A-flat verse over bowed bass and low clarinet. The clarinet takes the melody back on C and the piano re-enters in bar 14. Legato tracks share the corresponding soft clarinet recordings. Expand a folder to edit the notes and phrase expression. Bounce the Loop end marker with render_promenade.py.\nPiano score from Mutopia-2004/07/20-475 (public domain). Clarinet, bowed cellos and concert harp from Versilian Studios Chamber Orchestra 2 Community Edition (CC0), https://github.com/sgossner/VSCO-2-CE/tree/440300901dfe9275fd84e0b7763af1f8443ae62e . Grand piano from Salamander Grand Piano v3 by Alexander Holm, soft v4 recordings, https://github.com/sfzinstruments/SalamanderGrandPiano/tree/3382bf9496bba2486f5ab0de55a264d1dfc38404 , CC BY 3.0 https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/ .",
  "midi_originals": {}
}
